kakaotalk-debian-wrapper (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Wine patch: "Open folder" (explorer.exe /select, SHOpenFolderAndSelectItems)
    opens the Linux file manager and selects the file (FileManager1 D-Bus
    interface, falling back to xdg-open) instead of Wine's explorer.
  * Wine patch: file open/save dialogs (IFileDialog, GetOpenFileNameW,
    GetSaveFileNameW) use the Linux file chooser via xdg-desktop-portal,
    falling back to Wine's dialog when no portal is available. Folders picked
    outside the shared folders are linked into C:\Linux\, so saving there works
    without showing Wine's dialog again.
  * Wine patch: SHBrowseForFolderW uses the Linux file chooser too.
  * Launcher: enable both through the registry (TWEAKS_VERSION 6).
  * Recommend xdg-desktop-portal and dbus-send.

 -- kakaotalk-debian-wrapper contributors  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0900

kakaotalk-debian-wrapper (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Wine patch: composite GL content with alpha for windows that request
    DWM blur-behind, so notification popups and tooltips are no longer drawn
    with black borders.
  * Wine patch: pass the app minimum window size (WM_GETMINMAXINFO) to the
    window manager, so windows can no longer be shrunk to a thin line.
  * Enable camera (V4L2) support in the bundled Wine for video calls.
  * Korean font names (굴림, 돋움, 바탕, 궁서 and their -체 variants) are now
    substituted too, fixing broken Hangul in the classic installer EULA.
  * Open received files (images, videos, documents, hwp, ...) with the Linux
    default apps instead of Wine programs.
  * Limit the Linux folders visible to KakaoTalk to Downloads, Documents and
    Pictures and remove the Z: drive by default (KAKAOTALK_SHARED_DIRS,
    KAKAOTALK_FULL_ACCESS to change).
  * Launcher: kakaotalk --config (also in the app menu), kakaotalk --reset,
    kime/nimf detection, wait for the input method on autostart, GNOME tray
    extension hint.
  * README: input method status, tray icon notes, file access.

 -- kakaotalk-debian-wrapper contributors  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0900

kakaotalk-debian-wrapper (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Bundled Wine 11.0 (wow64, no i386 packages needed), built on Ubuntu 22.04.
  * Wine patch: ignore stale mouse move/resize requests so windows no longer
    stick to the pointer after dragging (KWin and others).
  * Supports both the classic KakaoTalk and the new Qt 6 based KakaoTalk.
  * Korean font substitution, DPI and input method (fcitx/ibus) setup.
  * Desktop entry, icon extracted from the user's install, kakaotalk:// links,
    optional autostart.

 -- kakaotalk-debian-wrapper contributors  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0900
